     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear group,<br><br>I would like to log new user sessions into a logging file using the package futile.logger. The reason here is that I want users to be able to configure the logging level themselves without me having to implement my own logging framework. The following is the beginning of my shinyServer function:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">shinyServer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">func </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    futile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">logger</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">flog</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">debug</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;New session at server.&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># is false: %s&quot;, toString(serverInfo()))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>    </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># only works in reactive environment..</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    futile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">logger</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">flog</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">debug</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;New session: %s&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> toString</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">session$clientData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">session$clientData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sep </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;: &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br>How can I wrap the call to session$clientData so that I can retrieve some information and put it in the log file?<br><br>I also appreciate any pointers to other ways to log to files from within a shiny server. <br><br>Thanks for your help!<br><br>/Daniel<br><br><br></div>"
